// <list> as seen through the Dinkum C++ Library 2.33. RECONSTRUCTION (PROPOSED by exe-ui-events-helper).
// Base: the stock VC6 <list> (node {_Next, _Prev, _Value}, layout allocator/_Head/_Size). Changed to what EE-AOC.exe
// proves (gWonNet's server list, std::list<WONAPI::SmartPtr<...>>; EEUIEWNSS*, 0x1eb7fb..0x1ebc13, and EEWonNet's
// out-of-line members 0xd17ea.., 0xd1e96, 0xd1eea, 0xd2df7, 0xd2e31):
//  - begin() checks the head: iterator(_Head == 0 ? 0 : _Next(_Head)) (0x1ebb77, inline copies in 0x1eb7fb..)
//  - insert(P, X) is a void _Insert(P, X) (0xd1e96: _Buynode(P, Prev(P)), _Incsize(1), construct, then link) plus a
//    wrapper returning --P; _Incsize(N) is out of line (0xd2e31)
//  - insert(P, F, L) and assign(F, L) are member templates dispatching on _Iter_cat(F) to _Insert(P, F, L, tag)
//    (0x1ebba0) and _Assign(F, L, tag) (0x1ebbc6: erase(begin(), end()), then insert); assign is 0x1ebb8b. The
//    forward-iterator _Insert carries the library's rollback (_TRY_BEGIN .. erase the inserted nodes): without /GX
//    the dead block still costs inline budget, which is what keeps it out of line (0x1ebba0)
//  - operator= is assign(_X.begin(), _X.end()) when this != &_X (inline in 0x1eb8a7)
//  - the copy ctor inserts through the member template (0x1ebb27)
// Members not yet proven keep the VC6 shapes.

